{title: Old Friend}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{comment_italic: Dedicated to those who carry invisible threads of support and love through all their lives.}

{start_of_verse}
Quiet rustle of paws in the hallway,
A torn ball is lying on the desk.
One who never once had been to the seaside
Is meeting his very last dawn on the earth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm not crying, oh no, I'm not crying.
Not silent, but sobbing behind.
And I thought it all was meant to be different.
My old friend is leaving in sleep.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
My gaze slides along the worn floorboards,
To the toys in the corner, on the floor.
Legs of chairs are singing their old song now.
Gently stroking: "sleep, sleep", I hum along.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm not crying, my friend, I'm not crying.
Every day for me is a gift.
And I thought it all would pass and like always
You would run off full speed far away.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Let me have, my dear friend, this one weakness,
Only out of the joy of those years.
In my heart you're alive, chasing like always
That old rubber ball out in the yard.
{end_of_verse}
